.TH SLIDESHOW\-LOCK 1 "2026-10-09" "slideshow\-lock" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slideshow\-lock \- idle slideshow screensaver that locks on input
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slideshow\-lock
.RB { service | settings | control | preview }
.RI [ argument " ...]"
.br
.B slideshow\-lock
.RB { \-h | \-\-help | help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slideshow\-lock
starts a full-screen picture slideshow on the screens of a GNOME session on
Wayland when the session has been idle, and locks the session when the user
touches the keyboard or the mouse. The pictures come from a folder, and the
settings have a window of their own.
.PP
.B slideshow\-lock
is the one command of the programs of the package. Its first argument names
the program; the arguments after it go to that program unchanged.
.B slideshow\-lock
.I command
.B \-\-help
lists the options of the program. Without a command, or with one that is not
listed below, it prints a usage text to the standard error and exits with
status 2.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B service
The service: it waits for the session to be idle, shows the slideshow, and
locks the session on the first input after the grace period and before the
machine suspends. The systemd user unit
.B slideshow\-lock.service
runs this command.
.TP
.B settings
The settings window alone.
.TP
.B control
Starts the service, then opens the settings window.
.BR slideshowlock (1)
is the short way to this command.
.TP
.B preview
The preview: the slideshow on every screen. Any key, click, scroll or mouse
movement ends it. It never locks the session.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "service"
These options replace the stored setting for this run of the service; they are
never written to the settings.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " FOLDER"
The picture folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-idle\-timeout " SECONDS"
Seconds of idle time before the slideshow starts, from 1 to 86400.
.TP
.BI \-\-grace " SECONDS"
Input within this many seconds after the slideshow has started does not lock
the session, from 0 to 86400.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECONDS"
Seconds per picture, from 1 to 86399.
.TP
.BI \-\-order " random" | name
The order of the pictures.
.TP
.BI \-\-scaling " fit" | fill
Fit the picture into the monitor, or fill the monitor with it.
.TP
.B \-\-pan
Scroll portrait pictures slowly (with fill).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Log every step.
.SS "preview"
These options replace the stored setting for this run of the preview; they are
never written to the settings.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " FOLDER"
The picture folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECONDS"
Seconds per picture, from 1 to 86399.
.TP
.BI \-\-order " random" | name
The order of the pictures.
.TP
.BI \-\-scaling " fit" | fill
Fit the picture into the monitor, or fill the monitor with it.
.TP
.B \-\-pan
Scroll portrait pictures slowly (with fill).
.TP
.BI \-\-transition " NAME"
How a picture changes into the next, or none. NAME is one of none, random,
crossfade, fade\-black, slide\-in, push, ken\-burns, zoom, wipe, circle, blur
and rotate.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Log every step.
.SS "settings"
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Log every step.
.SS "control"
.TP
.B autostart
For the start at login: the service is started, and the settings window opens
only the first time, when no picture folder has been chosen.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Log every step.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.B 0
on success, also for
.BR \-\-help .
.B 2
for no command or an unknown one, for a value out of its range, and for a
settings schema that is not installed. The exit status of
.B control
is described in
.BR slideshowlock (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/slideshow\-lock.service
The user unit of the service.
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/autostart/io.github.trensoft.slideshowlock.desktop
The autostart entry: it runs
.B slideshowlock autostart
at login (GNOME only).
.TP
.I /usr/share/slideshow\-lock/pictures
The seven sample pictures. At the first login they are copied once into the
folder
.I trensoft
in the pictures folder of the user.
.PP
The settings are stored in GSettings, in the schema
.B io.github.trensoft.slideshowlock
(path /io/github/trensoft/slideshowlock/).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The language of the interface comes from
.BR LANGUAGE ,
.BR LC_ALL ,
.B LC_MESSAGES
and
.BR LANG ,
in the order gettext reads them.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR slideshowlock (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
The project, with its documentation and its issue tracker:
.I https://github.com/trensoft/slideshow\-lock
.SH AUTHOR
TrenSoft. The code of this project was written with the help of AI agents.
